# What `gcloud builds submit` may upload.
#
# This is a DIFFERENT gate from .dockerignore and it runs earlier. gcloud tars the
# working directory and puts it in a Cloud Storage bucket before Docker sees any of it,
# so a file excluded from the image by .dockerignore can still end up sitting in GCS.
# Anything secret has to be listed in BOTH.
#
# Without this file gcloud invents one from .gitignore, which happens to cover .env
# today -- but relying on an implicit fallback to keep credentials out of a bucket is
# not a control, it is a coincidence.

# --- must never be uploaded -------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Operator data: owner maps carrying member emails and Discord ids, plus any
# credential exports or database dumps left in the working directory.
data/
*.dump
okie-local.dump

# --- pointless to upload ----------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes

node_modules
.next
out
build
coverage
*.tsbuildinfo

# Regenerated inside the builder from prisma/schema.prisma.
src/generated

.claude
.vscode
.idea
npm-debug.log*

# Credentials the GitHub auth action writes into the workspace. `builds submit`
# uploads the whole directory, so without this the file goes to Cloud Build.
gha-creds-*.json
